1
00:02:38,920 --> 00:02:41,640
Do you know that Korn is back?

2
00:02:41,720 --> 00:02:42,600
How did you find out?

3
00:02:42,680 --> 00:02:45,200
I talked to Mr. Nimit this morning.

4
00:02:45,800 --> 00:02:49,120
So you haven't been back
to your old home since you returned?

5
00:02:50,320 --> 00:02:53,040
Korn, go see Mom sometimes.

6
00:02:53,120 --> 00:02:54,440
She misses you so much.

7
00:02:57,160 --> 00:02:58,080
Oh, Rawee.

8
00:02:59,560 --> 00:03:01,280
Have you two met?

9
00:03:01,360 --> 00:03:02,760
Wait a minute.

10
00:03:04,520 --> 00:03:05,920
You two are brothers?

11
00:03:06,000 --> 00:03:07,560
Alyssa, you didn't know?

12
00:03:07,640 --> 00:03:10,080
Rawee and Phakorn grew up together.

13
00:03:10,160 --> 00:03:11,800
What kind of boyfriend are you?

14
00:03:11,880 --> 00:03:13,880
Why didn't you tell Alyssa?

15
00:03:13,960 --> 00:03:15,240
Hey, Alyssa.

16
00:03:18,640 --> 00:03:19,720
I'm here today

17
00:03:20,320 --> 00:03:23,120
as your friend
and as a partner of Tayawat Group.

18
00:03:23,200 --> 00:03:24,800
We talked about this, Korn.

19
00:03:24,880 --> 00:03:27,400
If I knew you'd introduce me
as your girlfriend,

20
00:03:27,480 --> 00:03:28,840
I wouldn't have come.

21
00:03:44,600 --> 00:03:45,680
What are you doing?

22
00:03:49,360 --> 00:03:51,240
I just tripped.

23
00:03:51,320 --> 00:03:52,880
Mr. Rawee was only helping me up.

24
00:03:53,800 --> 00:03:55,160
It's nothing, Korn.

25
00:04:00,440 --> 00:04:02,120
I was just startled.

26
00:04:02,200 --> 00:04:04,000
I didn't realize it was you.

27
00:04:04,080 --> 00:04:05,240
I'm sorry.

28
00:04:07,920 --> 00:04:08,920
It's okay.

29
00:04:09,720 --> 00:04:13,040
It's understandable not to recognize
someone after years apart.

30
00:04:18,360 --> 00:04:21,160
Thank you for helping me.

31
00:04:24,120 --> 00:04:25,120
You're welcome.

32
00:04:33,960 --> 00:04:37,440
Hey, Alyssa. I didn't mean to.

33
00:04:37,520 --> 00:04:38,800
I didn't know it was Wee.

34
00:04:38,880 --> 00:04:40,800
I thought it was another male employee.

35
00:04:42,080 --> 00:04:43,920
Whoever it was,
you shouldn't have pushed him.

36
00:04:44,960 --> 00:04:46,160
You're right. I'm sorry.

37
00:04:46,880 --> 00:04:49,920
-The person you should apologize to--
-I already apologized to Wee.

38
00:04:50,000 --> 00:04:53,640
He's my older brother.
He knows I didn't mean to do it.

39
00:04:55,480 --> 00:04:56,400
Okay.

40
00:04:57,640 --> 00:04:59,200
I'm done with this.

41
00:04:59,960 --> 00:05:02,040
I'll head to the meeting.
Aunt Da is waiting.

42
00:05:04,000 --> 00:05:05,280
Alyssa.

43
00:05:06,240 --> 00:05:08,560
After the meeting,
let's have lunch together.

44
00:05:37,240 --> 00:05:39,200
Oh, there you are.

45
00:05:40,560 --> 00:05:42,240
-Can I help you?
-Whoa.

46
00:05:42,320 --> 00:05:44,360
Making coffee? It smells so good.

47
00:05:45,080 --> 00:05:47,600
-Would you like a cup?
-Oh, that'd be nice.

48
00:05:47,680 --> 00:05:50,080
-It'll wake me up.
-Sure.

49
00:05:50,160 --> 00:05:51,480
-Thanks.
-No problem.

50
00:05:52,080 --> 00:05:53,080
Wow.

51
00:05:55,080 --> 00:05:56,200
It smells great.

52
00:05:57,240 --> 00:05:59,520
Oh, Wee! I almost forgot.

53
00:05:59,600 --> 00:06:01,800
I came to get you for your introduction.

54
00:06:02,840 --> 00:06:03,840
Introduction?

55
00:06:05,160 --> 00:06:07,520
-With whom?
-With your new boss.

56
00:06:20,120 --> 00:06:21,080
Wee.

57
00:06:22,080 --> 00:06:25,560
I found a way for us to stay close

58
00:06:25,640 --> 00:06:27,400
without worrying about anyone finding out.

59
00:06:29,120 --> 00:06:30,400
So what do you want me to do?

60
00:06:32,840 --> 00:06:35,560
Come be my assistant.

61
00:06:35,640 --> 00:06:37,360
Be my shadow.

62
00:06:40,240 --> 00:06:43,320
Why? Aren't you happy?

63
00:06:45,120 --> 00:06:47,920
Are you still upset with me about earlier?

64
00:06:49,240 --> 00:06:50,520
I'm sorry.

65
00:06:51,240 --> 00:06:54,880
You don't have to apologize to me, Korn.
I'm not upset with you at all.

66
00:06:56,200 --> 00:06:58,440
Has Ms. Nada agreed to it yet?

67
00:07:02,760 --> 00:07:06,600
If our mother found out
we were working together,

68
00:07:07,200 --> 00:07:10,040
she'd be so happy. Don't you think?

69
00:07:14,280 --> 00:07:16,600
<i>Mom, we're finally working together.</i>

70
00:07:19,280 --> 00:07:21,640
That's good. Take good care of each other.

71
00:07:21,720 --> 00:07:23,440
Help each other whenever you can.

72
00:07:23,520 --> 00:07:25,240
If something bothers you,

73
00:07:25,320 --> 00:07:27,280
talk it out and understand each other.

74
00:07:27,360 --> 00:07:28,720
Don't leave things unresolved.

75
00:07:29,480 --> 00:07:30,840
<i>-Yes, Mom.</i>
-Yes.

76
00:07:32,200 --> 00:07:33,560
<i>Mom.</i>

77
00:07:33,640 --> 00:07:36,760
<i>When we're free,</i>
<i>we'll come home for dinner.</i>

78
00:07:36,840 --> 00:07:38,440
<i>I miss your cooking.</i>

79
00:07:39,400 --> 00:07:41,440
<i>Of course. Come anytime.</i>

80
00:07:41,520 --> 00:07:44,520
<i>I miss you so much, Korn.</i>

81
00:07:45,040 --> 00:07:47,960
<i>Alright, we'll get back to work now.</i>

82
00:07:48,040 --> 00:07:50,600
<i>We need to start working.</i>
<i>We'll talk again later.</i>

83
00:07:51,200 --> 00:07:52,480
Okay.

84
00:07:53,000 --> 00:07:54,280
<i>-Bye.</i>
<i>-Bye.</i>

85
00:08:01,400 --> 00:08:04,080
Wait, I have something for you.

86
00:08:12,720 --> 00:08:14,880
Hey, no.

87
00:08:16,480 --> 00:08:19,080
I'm not giving you the car.
I want you to drive me.

88
00:08:19,640 --> 00:08:21,720
I just sent

89
00:08:21,800 --> 00:08:23,000
the company driver back.

90
00:08:24,800 --> 00:08:27,560
So you want me to be your driver?

91
00:08:31,600 --> 00:08:34,000
Then we can sneak away and go somewhere

92
00:08:34,080 --> 00:08:35,880
without worrying about anyone finding out.

93
00:08:38,520 --> 00:08:40,080
You're really something.

94
00:08:53,760 --> 00:08:54,760
Come in.

95
00:09:10,280 --> 00:09:12,520
-Kong.
-Wee.

96
00:09:15,320 --> 00:09:16,480
What are you doing here?

97
00:09:16,560 --> 00:09:18,800
I should be asking you that.

98
00:09:19,400 --> 00:09:22,080
I just started here.
I'm driving for one of the executives.

99
00:09:22,160 --> 00:09:24,840
Really? I work here too.

100
00:09:24,920 --> 00:09:26,200
Who are you driving for?

101
00:09:27,200 --> 00:09:29,280
Mr. Panas. You know him?

102
00:09:30,320 --> 00:09:31,560
He's my boss's younger brother.

103
00:09:33,120 --> 00:09:34,400
Who's your boss?

104
00:09:35,000 --> 00:09:36,000
Ms. Nada.

105
00:09:41,880 --> 00:09:44,080
Wee.

106
00:09:44,720 --> 00:09:46,240
I'm warning you.

107
00:09:47,040 --> 00:09:48,840
Stay away from Ms. Nada.

108
00:09:54,360 --> 00:09:58,600
MS. NADA TAYAWAT - COO
TAYAWAT GROUP PUBLIC COMPANY LIMITED

109
00:10:03,960 --> 00:10:07,320
Thank you for honoring our small company
by working with us.

110
00:10:08,440 --> 00:10:11,560
Small? Not at all.
You're already a top-ten company.

111
00:10:13,520 --> 00:10:15,040
I'm happy to be working with you.

112
00:10:16,480 --> 00:10:19,960
It's strange. I never thought
I'd work with your father's generation,

113
00:10:20,040 --> 00:10:22,040
but now

114
00:10:22,120 --> 00:10:23,760
we're partners.

115
00:10:27,640 --> 00:10:30,440
Is there something between you and Phakorn
that I don't know about?

116
00:10:34,640 --> 00:10:35,840
We're friends.

117
00:10:37,680 --> 00:10:40,080
Phakorn is so sweet and clingy.

118
00:10:40,760 --> 00:10:43,040
What do they call it these days?

119
00:10:43,120 --> 00:10:44,480
The puppy type.

120
00:10:45,480 --> 00:10:47,240
If you like that kind, he's perfect.

121
00:10:50,720 --> 00:10:51,680
Yes.

122
00:10:57,560 --> 00:10:59,080
Time's up for the workaholic.

123
00:11:04,000 --> 00:11:05,520
You always know the time.

124
00:11:06,560 --> 00:11:08,480
Taddao sent word

125
00:11:08,560 --> 00:11:09,760
that the meeting is over.

126
00:11:09,840 --> 00:11:11,400
So I came to pick Alyssa up for lunch.

127
00:11:12,480 --> 00:11:13,360
Alright.

128
00:11:14,680 --> 00:11:15,880
Want to come with us, Mom?

129
00:11:17,160 --> 00:11:18,040
You two go ahead.

130
00:11:22,080 --> 00:11:22,960
Let's go.

131
00:11:27,600 --> 00:11:29,200
-Goodbye.
-Excuse us.

132
00:11:35,120 --> 00:11:36,000
Goodbye.

133
00:11:53,560 --> 00:11:54,840
Congratulations, Da.

134
00:11:55,880 --> 00:11:57,840
You managed to close
the Sea Sand Sun project.

135
00:11:58,760 --> 00:12:00,760
With the condo market oversaturated,

136
00:12:01,560 --> 00:12:02,760
you still sold everything.

137
00:12:03,680 --> 00:12:05,080
You're really amazing.

138
00:12:08,160 --> 00:12:10,080
Are you going
to the project closing party?

139
00:12:11,800 --> 00:12:13,920
Why? Do you want to go?

140
00:12:15,640 --> 00:12:16,880
If I wanted to go,

141
00:12:18,000 --> 00:12:19,240
would you invite me?

142
00:12:20,720 --> 00:12:22,080
Taddao.

143
00:12:22,160 --> 00:12:23,920
-Handle it.
-Yes.

144
00:12:25,560 --> 00:12:27,920
-Should I pick you up?
-No.

145
00:12:28,520 --> 00:12:29,920
I'm going with Korn.

146
00:12:30,000 --> 00:12:31,040
Korn is coming too?

147
00:12:33,320 --> 00:12:34,280
Then that's perfect.

148
00:12:35,080 --> 00:12:36,800
I wanted to get closer to Korn anyway.

149
00:12:40,000 --> 00:12:42,080
Just don't get him into trouble.

150
00:12:44,200 --> 00:12:45,280
Don't worry.

151
00:12:46,320 --> 00:12:47,840
I'll take good care of him.

152
00:12:51,120 --> 00:12:52,680
Someone is waiting for you in the room.

153
00:12:56,480 --> 00:12:58,520
<i>Your son has good taste too.</i>

154
00:12:59,120 --> 00:13:00,560
Choosing to date a rich girl.

155
00:13:01,920 --> 00:13:04,400
They may be wealthy provincials,

156
00:13:06,320 --> 00:13:08,560
but this family is truly wealthy.

157
00:13:08,640 --> 00:13:09,960
I can vouch for that.

158
00:13:11,040 --> 00:13:12,760
Did you need something from me, Father?

159
00:13:13,920 --> 00:13:15,760
Hey, but I support it.

160
00:13:16,840 --> 00:13:18,840
She's the niece of my close friend.

161
00:13:18,920 --> 00:13:21,840
If he wants to pursue her, let me know.

162
00:13:21,920 --> 00:13:23,160
I'll help.

163
00:13:25,360 --> 00:13:27,080
Have you forgotten

164
00:13:27,160 --> 00:13:29,960
that Alyssa's father is close to me?

165
00:13:30,560 --> 00:13:32,080
Better to go through her father,

166
00:13:32,160 --> 00:13:33,880
not his aunt.

167
00:13:36,000 --> 00:13:38,400
Is there something
you want to confess to me?

168
00:13:40,200 --> 00:13:41,600
Confess what?

169
00:13:47,120 --> 00:13:48,800
-Leave first.
-No need.

170
00:13:49,400 --> 00:13:52,960
This concerns that secretary of yours.

171
00:13:59,800 --> 00:14:02,200
Look at this and explain yourself.

172
00:14:02,800 --> 00:14:05,680
Why did you secretly buy up
so many shares behind Father's back?

173
00:14:11,240 --> 00:14:14,440
SYMBOL: TYWG TYPE: BUY
VOLUME: 2,000,000 PRICE: 25.00

174
00:14:17,280 --> 00:14:19,000
Before you came,

175
00:14:19,080 --> 00:14:21,480
did you see this document, Father?

176
00:14:38,680 --> 00:14:39,880
Hey.

177
00:14:39,960 --> 00:14:41,640
What exactly are you planning, Nada?

178
00:14:43,160 --> 00:14:45,800
And why did you use
your secretary's husband's name

179
00:14:45,880 --> 00:14:47,960
to buy up so many shares?

180
00:14:48,720 --> 00:14:52,040
I can explain this, Ma'am.

181
00:14:52,120 --> 00:14:55,440
The reason my husband bought them
was because I suggested it.

182
00:14:55,520 --> 00:14:57,760
It had nothing to do with Ms. Nada.

183
00:14:57,840 --> 00:15:00,440
Well, I believed

184
00:15:01,040 --> 00:15:03,960
the Pattaya condo project would sell out,

185
00:15:04,040 --> 00:15:06,160
and I was confident the shares would rise,

186
00:15:06,240 --> 00:15:08,720
so I asked my husband to buy them.

187
00:15:08,800 --> 00:15:09,760
Really?

188
00:15:11,400 --> 00:15:13,120
Your husband is wealthy enough

189
00:15:13,200 --> 00:15:15,480
to buy millions worth of shares?

190
00:15:16,400 --> 00:15:18,960
Pim, you're not

191
00:15:19,040 --> 00:15:20,640
the only wealthy person in this country.

192
00:15:21,480 --> 00:15:24,520
The world is much bigger than you think.

193
00:15:24,600 --> 00:15:27,320
Step out of your shell
and see it for yourself.

194
00:15:27,400 --> 00:15:28,480
I'm asking you.

195
00:15:31,720 --> 00:15:32,720
If there's nothing else,

196
00:15:32,800 --> 00:15:35,120
-I'll leave you to it.
-Father.

197
00:15:36,000 --> 00:15:38,000
This isn't how we discussed it.

198
00:15:38,840 --> 00:15:41,160
A stake this small doesn't interest me.

199
00:15:41,760 --> 00:15:42,880
Besides,

200
00:15:42,960 --> 00:15:45,560
it doesn't affect the board at all.

201
00:15:46,160 --> 00:15:47,520
I don't understand

202
00:15:47,600 --> 00:15:50,240
why you and Pim are so worried.

203
00:15:54,040 --> 00:15:55,480
Are you afraid Da
will take the family fortune?

204
00:15:56,600 --> 00:15:57,680
Isn't that true?

205
00:15:57,760 --> 00:15:58,760
At this point,

206
00:15:58,840 --> 00:16:01,960
I'm practically
the owner of this company already.

207
00:16:02,800 --> 00:16:06,200
There's no reason for me
to take over my own company.

208
00:16:06,800 --> 00:16:09,560
Enough. Stop fighting.

209
00:16:10,360 --> 00:16:12,440
-Nothing's wrong, so that's fine.
-Father.

210
00:16:13,040 --> 00:16:14,600
But this isn't what we discussed.

211
00:16:15,200 --> 00:16:16,480
Come on, Pim.

212
00:16:17,320 --> 00:16:19,240
Stop putting ideas in Father's head.

213
00:16:19,840 --> 00:16:22,240
Da already has enough headaches from work.

214
00:16:24,480 --> 00:16:25,360
Let's go, Father.

215
00:16:44,200 --> 00:16:46,440
I'm sorry for causing trouble for you,
Ms. Nada.

216
00:16:46,520 --> 00:16:47,840
This was my fault.

217
00:16:48,800 --> 00:16:52,200
Tell your husband to sell them quickly.
The price will drop soon.

218
00:17:02,520 --> 00:17:03,400
Move aside.

219
00:17:04,079 --> 00:17:05,280
Father.

220
00:17:06,520 --> 00:17:08,440
Why do we have to put up
with her this much?

221
00:17:09,040 --> 00:17:10,640
It's obvious something isn't right.

222
00:17:11,920 --> 00:17:13,040
Pim.

223
00:17:13,640 --> 00:17:16,680
If you're going after Da,
you need to be more careful.

224
00:17:17,560 --> 00:17:18,760
Hey.

225
00:17:18,839 --> 00:17:21,599
Even if the shares we found
are less than one percent,

226
00:17:21,680 --> 00:17:23,800
what about the rest we don't know about?

227
00:17:25,480 --> 00:17:26,920
Father.

228
00:17:27,000 --> 00:17:29,160
Do you really think Nada works this hard

229
00:17:29,240 --> 00:17:30,960
and expects nothing?

230
00:17:31,760 --> 00:17:34,440
No way. She definitely wants something.

231
00:17:35,440 --> 00:17:37,000
And what have you done?

232
00:17:37,800 --> 00:17:39,600
What do you do all day, huh?

233
00:17:40,200 --> 00:17:41,400
Father.

234
00:17:41,480 --> 00:17:43,240
Find more evidence.

235
00:17:44,000 --> 00:17:46,520
I'm already tired
from giving in to you today.

236
00:17:46,600 --> 00:17:48,400
-Father!
-Shut up.

237
00:18:11,840 --> 00:18:14,200
Shouldn't you sit up front
with your brother? It might look bad.

238
00:18:15,080 --> 00:18:17,000
Right now, Wee is still my assistant.

239
00:18:19,520 --> 00:18:21,280
Does being an assistant
include driving too?

240
00:18:23,360 --> 00:18:24,840
Just sit in the back.

241
00:18:26,080 --> 00:18:28,920
Please get in quickly.
I don't want to attract attention.

242
00:18:34,120 --> 00:18:35,360
Thank you.

243
00:19:10,800 --> 00:19:11,800
Thank you.

244
00:19:13,720 --> 00:19:16,200
Wee, just leave the car here
and take a ride back

245
00:19:16,280 --> 00:19:17,920
to the office. No need to wait.

246
00:19:18,520 --> 00:19:19,440
Huh?

247
00:19:20,520 --> 00:19:21,960
You're not staying for lunch with us?

248
00:19:23,000 --> 00:19:25,600
It's okay.
I have a lot of unfinished work.

249
00:19:39,080 --> 00:19:42,560
It feels like you're trying
to keep your brother down somehow.

250
00:19:44,600 --> 00:19:46,120
I knew you'd think that.

251
00:19:46,760 --> 00:19:49,080
Other than us, no one knows

252
00:19:49,160 --> 00:19:50,720
we're brothers.

253
00:19:51,880 --> 00:19:53,920
And if people start talking
about connections,

254
00:19:54,000 --> 00:19:55,760
Wee definitely won't be happy.

255
00:19:58,600 --> 00:19:59,600
That's true.

256
00:20:00,960 --> 00:20:03,120
I'm not the type to succeed
and forget my family.

257
00:20:05,240 --> 00:20:07,640
Alright, you pass.

258
00:20:10,200 --> 00:20:11,480
There's a checklist too?

259
00:20:41,000 --> 00:20:42,000
Here you go.

260
00:20:43,480 --> 00:20:44,840
Thank you.

261
00:20:46,360 --> 00:20:47,360
Excuse me.

262
00:20:54,000 --> 00:20:55,800
Thank you. Bye.

263
00:21:07,440 --> 00:21:08,680
What is this?

264
00:21:08,760 --> 00:21:10,720
I had no idea about any of this.

265
00:21:10,800 --> 00:21:12,880
You really have good taste.

266
00:21:12,960 --> 00:21:14,800
And he's from the Tayawat family too.

267
00:21:17,040 --> 00:21:19,800
Korn is Aunt Walai's adopted son.

268
00:21:20,560 --> 00:21:21,920
I thought you didn't like them?

269
00:21:22,520 --> 00:21:25,440
It's okay. The past is the past.

270
00:21:25,520 --> 00:21:27,440
I live in the present.

271
00:21:28,240 --> 00:21:29,280
Let me make it clear.

272
00:21:29,880 --> 00:21:34,160
This one has my approval.
I'm rooting for you two.

273
00:21:35,320 --> 00:21:37,560
We're just getting to know each other.

274
00:21:38,720 --> 00:21:41,400
People call it
getting to know each other these days?

275
00:21:41,480 --> 00:21:44,240
Back in my day,
we called it seeing someone.

276
00:21:46,240 --> 00:21:48,120
It doesn't matter
if you're just getting to know each other

277
00:21:48,200 --> 00:21:50,120
or already dating.

278
00:21:50,200 --> 00:21:52,080
As long as you two keep seeing each other,

279
00:21:52,160 --> 00:21:53,400
I'm happy.

280
00:21:54,560 --> 00:21:56,960
Also, your father

281
00:21:57,040 --> 00:21:58,720
will come see you in a few days.

282
00:22:00,320 --> 00:22:01,840
You shared the news with Dad too?

283
00:22:01,920 --> 00:22:03,320
Not just your dad.

284
00:22:03,400 --> 00:22:06,000
I shared it in every Line group.

285
00:22:06,080 --> 00:22:08,040
And I posted it on Facebook too.

286
00:22:08,120 --> 00:22:09,680
Don't forget to like it, okay?

287
00:22:10,200 --> 00:22:12,280
Oh my god.

288
00:22:31,520 --> 00:22:33,200
<i>What kind of CSR is this?</i>

289
00:22:33,280 --> 00:22:36,320
<i>Major real estate company</i>
<i>linked to famous fortune teller.</i>

290
00:22:36,400 --> 00:22:39,800
They announced a CSR donation
to help society.

291
00:22:39,880 --> 00:22:40,920
But which society?

292
00:22:41,000 --> 00:22:43,400
The money went to a famous fortune teller

293
00:22:43,480 --> 00:22:45,400
accused of embezzling temple funds.

294
00:22:45,480 --> 00:22:48,720
The amount wasn't much. Just eight digits.

295
00:22:49,920 --> 00:22:52,720
Tens, hundreds, thousands, ten-thousands,
hundred-thousands, millions.

296
00:22:54,040 --> 00:22:55,560
How many tens of millions is that?

297
00:22:56,160 --> 00:22:59,760
Alyssa, can you help me check something?
The comments say

298
00:22:59,840 --> 00:23:01,880
it's Tayawat Group.

299
00:23:01,960 --> 00:23:03,240
Is that true? Take a look.

300
00:23:06,560 --> 00:23:09,560
THEY ANNOUNCED A CSR DONATION
TO HELP SOCIETY, BUT WHICH SOCIETY?

301
00:23:19,680 --> 00:23:21,800
Please wait a moment
for the meeting documents.

302
00:23:22,680 --> 00:23:24,280
I'd like to have Rawee,

303
00:23:24,360 --> 00:23:26,320
my new assistant, join the meeting.

304
00:23:26,400 --> 00:23:28,280
He'll need to be involved anyway.

305
00:23:28,360 --> 00:23:30,480
-New assistant?
-Yes.

306
00:23:31,120 --> 00:23:32,520
-Rawee?
-Yes.

307
00:23:32,600 --> 00:23:35,440
He's the older brother
who grew up with Phakorn.

308
00:23:35,520 --> 00:23:37,240
He's currently helping Phakorn.

309
00:23:39,200 --> 00:23:40,080
Go ahead.

310
00:23:40,600 --> 00:23:42,720
I'd like to hear
the younger generation's opinions too.

311
00:23:44,040 --> 00:23:45,360
Father.

312
00:23:45,880 --> 00:23:48,920
But this is a special family meeting.

313
00:23:53,720 --> 00:23:55,120
Yes.

314
00:23:55,200 --> 00:23:56,440
I'll go get him myself.

315
00:23:57,280 --> 00:23:58,280
Yes.

316
00:24:22,000 --> 00:24:23,240
Korn.

317
00:24:24,280 --> 00:24:25,240
Not in the meeting yet?

318
00:24:25,920 --> 00:24:27,720
Mom sent me to get you for the meeting.

319
00:24:29,240 --> 00:24:31,400
Did you do anything to make her notice?

320
00:24:32,000 --> 00:24:34,040
Why does she suddenly want you
in the meeting?

321
00:24:34,680 --> 00:24:36,080
Why would I do that, Korn?

322
00:24:37,920 --> 00:24:40,800
Stop being suspicious of me. It hurts.

323
00:24:44,440 --> 00:24:45,840
Then hurry and go to the meeting.

324
00:24:46,400 --> 00:24:48,080
They'll get annoyed
if you keep them waiting.

325
00:24:50,680 --> 00:24:52,720
Wait, Korn.
Aren't you coming to the meeting too?

326
00:24:58,520 --> 00:24:59,960
I'm not that important.

327
00:25:00,680 --> 00:25:02,040
I need to make a call.

328
00:25:23,960 --> 00:25:25,080
Excuse me.

329
00:25:26,120 --> 00:25:26,960
Come sit down.

330
00:25:41,120 --> 00:25:44,400
Phakorn is on a call. He's on his way.

331
00:25:46,640 --> 00:25:49,440
We keep waiting and waiting.
We'll never get this meeting started.

332
00:25:50,120 --> 00:25:50,960
Let's begin.

333
00:25:51,800 --> 00:25:52,800
Yes.

334
00:25:56,480 --> 00:25:59,640
Have you found out where this came from?

335
00:26:00,240 --> 00:26:01,280
Yes.

336
00:26:02,200 --> 00:26:03,880
It came from this news outlet.

337
00:26:04,480 --> 00:26:06,200
BREAKING! PIMPA TAYAWAT EXPOSED
AS THE PERSON BEHIND FAKE CSR DONATIONS

338
00:26:06,800 --> 00:26:10,080
Earlier, there was news
that this fortune teller

339
00:26:10,160 --> 00:26:11,280
had been arrested.

340
00:26:11,880 --> 00:26:13,760
So people traced the money trail

341
00:26:13,840 --> 00:26:16,840
until they found a donation made
under our company's name.

342
00:26:18,360 --> 00:26:20,840
I don't remember
why this didn't become news back then.

343
00:26:20,920 --> 00:26:23,440
Because I paid to keep the news quiet.

344
00:26:23,520 --> 00:26:26,000
Then why didn't you pay
to keep it quiet again?

345
00:26:26,080 --> 00:26:28,080
It happened a long time ago.

346
00:26:28,160 --> 00:26:29,440
Who would have thought

347
00:26:29,520 --> 00:26:31,920
someone would dig this mistake up again?

348
00:26:33,560 --> 00:26:36,000
Instead of asking
why I didn't keep the news quiet,

349
00:26:36,080 --> 00:26:37,400
ask yourself

350
00:26:37,480 --> 00:26:39,840
why you used the company's CSR budget

351
00:26:39,920 --> 00:26:41,440
to donate to that fortune teller.

352
00:26:41,520 --> 00:26:43,800
I still haven't gotten an answer.

353
00:26:44,400 --> 00:26:46,600
Father already punished me
for that back then.

354
00:26:46,680 --> 00:26:48,080
Why blame me again?

355
00:26:48,160 --> 00:26:50,320
Shouldn't we focus on fixing this instead?

356
00:26:50,400 --> 00:26:53,160
Then figure out
how to deal with the news, Pim.

357
00:26:53,240 --> 00:26:54,960
The evidence is already so clear.

358
00:26:56,240 --> 00:26:58,840
For us, this amount of money
isn't a big deal.

359
00:26:58,920 --> 00:27:01,600
But if the board finds out,

360
00:27:01,680 --> 00:27:04,320
I can already tell they won't be happy

361
00:27:04,400 --> 00:27:07,080
that your name is still on the board.

362
00:27:07,160 --> 00:27:09,720
Nada, what do you mean by that?

363
00:27:09,800 --> 00:27:11,200
Are you trying to remove me?

364
00:27:11,800 --> 00:27:13,880
I'm having the legal team check

365
00:27:13,960 --> 00:27:15,800
whether this violates the law.

366
00:27:18,040 --> 00:27:19,440
Even if it's not illegal,

367
00:27:20,080 --> 00:27:22,680
it could still affect our new projects.

368
00:27:23,480 --> 00:27:25,000
At the very least, our credibility.

369
00:27:36,360 --> 00:27:38,000
The legal team has confirmed

370
00:27:38,080 --> 00:27:39,520
that it doesn't violate any laws

371
00:27:39,600 --> 00:27:40,560
because the donation

372
00:27:40,640 --> 00:27:43,040
was transferred directly
to the temple's account.

373
00:27:43,120 --> 00:27:45,600
We're also considered victims
in this matter.

374
00:27:47,280 --> 00:27:48,560
What do you want to do, Nada?

375
00:27:51,440 --> 00:27:54,160
I think it's better to stay quiet.

376
00:27:54,240 --> 00:27:56,160
Once that famous fortune teller
is arrested,

377
00:27:56,240 --> 00:27:57,520
it'll die down on its own.

378
00:27:58,960 --> 00:28:01,760
I agree. If we don't give interviews,

379
00:28:01,840 --> 00:28:03,240
there won't be any more news.

380
00:28:05,880 --> 00:28:07,160
What do you think, Rawee?

381
00:28:12,760 --> 00:28:14,080
You want my opinion?

382
00:28:14,160 --> 00:28:15,800
Of course.

383
00:28:16,560 --> 00:28:18,760
I want to hear
the younger generation's perspective too.

384
00:28:22,120 --> 00:28:24,760
I think you should make a statement
and clarify the facts.

385
00:28:31,040 --> 00:28:33,000
So we just make ourselves look stupid?

386
00:28:37,480 --> 00:28:38,760
Finish what you were saying.

387
00:28:41,760 --> 00:28:44,000
Even though the truth
is a personal matter,

388
00:28:44,080 --> 00:28:46,400
the news was reported
in the company's name.

389
00:28:47,000 --> 00:28:48,640
I think if you handle it this way,

390
00:28:49,520 --> 00:28:52,400
the image of the company and yourself
will appear more dignified.

391
00:28:53,800 --> 00:28:56,400
Right now, many media outlets
are digging into companies,

392
00:28:56,480 --> 00:28:58,360
celebrities, and politicians.

393
00:28:59,000 --> 00:29:01,560
I don't think this news
will disappear that easily.

394
00:29:02,160 --> 00:29:03,400
That's an interesting point.

395
00:29:04,480 --> 00:29:06,120
That makes it two votes to one.

396
00:29:14,680 --> 00:29:16,200
I'd like to cast my vote too, Grandpa.

397
00:29:22,360 --> 00:29:24,880
I agree with Mom and Uncle.

398
00:29:25,680 --> 00:29:28,040
I'm worried
that if we admit fault in a statement,

399
00:29:28,120 --> 00:29:29,680
it will open the door

400
00:29:29,760 --> 00:29:31,200
to endless digging.

401
00:29:32,000 --> 00:29:34,880
And I'm worried
it could affect our family name too.

402
00:29:35,760 --> 00:29:36,960
I think we should stay quiet

403
00:29:37,040 --> 00:29:40,360
and have a team negotiate with the media
to kill the story

404
00:29:40,960 --> 00:29:42,720
in exchange for advertising.

405
00:29:43,840 --> 00:29:46,080
Besides, public attention these days

406
00:29:46,160 --> 00:29:47,880
changes very quickly.

407
00:29:47,960 --> 00:29:49,560
I don't think anyone will focus

408
00:29:49,640 --> 00:29:51,120
on our company for that long.

409
00:29:52,480 --> 00:29:54,360
That's an interesting approach too.

410
00:29:57,040 --> 00:29:58,360
I agree with Korn.

411
00:29:59,280 --> 00:30:01,640
No need to make a statement
and create more trouble.

412
00:30:02,600 --> 00:30:04,080
Three votes to one.

413
00:30:04,920 --> 00:30:06,520
Let's go with this.

414
00:30:08,200 --> 00:30:10,840
Do I even have a vote, Father?

415
00:30:11,560 --> 00:30:13,840
Everyone already thinks
I'm the one at fault anyway.

416
00:30:16,000 --> 00:30:18,400
I hope you listen to your family

417
00:30:19,440 --> 00:30:20,960
more than outsiders.

418
00:30:33,960 --> 00:30:35,280
That Nada

419
00:30:35,360 --> 00:30:38,360
must be planning
to get me removed from my position.

420
00:30:42,040 --> 00:30:43,800
What did you do to her?

421
00:30:45,920 --> 00:30:48,680
It's because I told Father
she was hiding shares.

422
00:30:48,760 --> 00:30:50,400
Compared to your other moves,

423
00:30:50,480 --> 00:30:52,280
this one is pretty infuriating.

424
00:30:56,520 --> 00:30:57,920
Hey, Panas.

425
00:30:58,640 --> 00:31:00,840
Don't you think Nada

426
00:31:00,920 --> 00:31:03,040
cares too much about that kid?

427
00:31:04,320 --> 00:31:05,160
What kid?

428
00:31:06,360 --> 00:31:09,560
The kid who grew up
in the same house as Phakorn.

429
00:31:13,560 --> 00:31:15,440
The kid whose name sounds like Rawich?

430
00:31:16,720 --> 00:31:17,560
Rawich.

431
00:31:18,720 --> 00:31:21,080
Rawee. Oh, right.

432
00:31:21,800 --> 00:31:23,360
Their names really do sound alike.

433
00:31:25,560 --> 00:31:26,880
But seriously,

434
00:31:26,960 --> 00:31:29,200
he kind of looks like him too.

435
00:31:32,960 --> 00:31:36,080
-Don't tell me that kid is…
-Isn't it true?

436
00:31:42,520 --> 00:31:44,200
This is getting interesting.

437
00:31:53,360 --> 00:31:56,240
Yes. That's why I called to ask you, Wee.

438
00:31:56,320 --> 00:31:58,320
Have you had a chance
to see or talk to him at all?

439
00:32:01,760 --> 00:32:03,280
Korn has been pretty busy lately.

440
00:32:04,000 --> 00:32:05,760
He just launched a new project.

441
00:32:05,840 --> 00:32:06,720
Really?

442
00:32:08,000 --> 00:32:09,680
That's what I thought too.

443
00:32:09,760 --> 00:32:12,560
But I can't help feeling a little hurt.

444
00:32:13,280 --> 00:32:15,280
<i>I just talked to Korn.</i>

445
00:32:15,360 --> 00:32:17,320
He was still telling me he missed you.

446
00:32:18,840 --> 00:32:20,160
When he's free,

447
00:32:20,240 --> 00:32:22,280
I'll take him back home to stay over.

448
00:32:26,120 --> 00:32:27,800
Wee, please help your brother.

449
00:32:30,120 --> 00:32:32,160
Your youngest son is more than capable.

450
00:32:33,400 --> 00:32:35,120
He hardly needs my help at all.

451
00:32:37,360 --> 00:32:40,360
But the social circle he's in now
is very different from ours.

452
00:32:40,440 --> 00:32:43,320
I'm worried he won't be able to adjust.

453
00:32:43,400 --> 00:32:46,320
<i>You two are brothers.</i>
<i>You have to love each other.</i>

454
00:32:47,960 --> 00:32:50,000
Even if Korn has a new family now…

455
00:32:52,120 --> 00:32:54,680
But we all know how things really are.

456
00:32:54,760 --> 00:32:57,240
<i>In the end, if the truth comes out,</i>

457
00:32:57,840 --> 00:33:00,920
he'll only have us.
Don't abandon him, Wee.

458
00:33:01,520 --> 00:33:03,440
Why would I do that?

459
00:33:04,400 --> 00:33:05,640
Because in the end,

460
00:33:06,240 --> 00:33:08,800
I only have you and Korn too.

461
00:33:11,720 --> 00:33:12,720
Okay.

462
00:33:34,080 --> 00:33:35,120
Thank you.

463
00:34:08,440 --> 00:34:11,360
Why didn't you tell me
you were renting her father's house?

464
00:34:14,800 --> 00:34:16,400
I didn't see why I needed to tell you.

465
00:34:17,000 --> 00:34:18,480
You never asked.

466
00:34:18,560 --> 00:34:20,120
And I'm not even close to her.

467
00:34:21,440 --> 00:34:23,400
But you knew I was seeing Alyssa.

468
00:34:23,480 --> 00:34:26,360
Whether you're close or not,
you should've told me.

469
00:34:26,440 --> 00:34:28,280
It's not a big deal.

470
00:34:28,360 --> 00:34:30,239
But it is a big deal to me.

471
00:34:31,040 --> 00:34:33,239
Okay. I'm sorry.

472
00:34:34,159 --> 00:34:36,840
Are you apologizing for this
or what happened this afternoon?

473
00:34:37,840 --> 00:34:40,440
So you're upset with me
about earlier, right?

474
00:34:42,159 --> 00:34:45,040
I'm going home so you can get some rest.

475
00:34:45,639 --> 00:34:48,440
Wait, Korn. Korn!

476
00:34:49,760 --> 00:34:50,800
Korn!

477
00:35:02,400 --> 00:35:03,360
Yes.

478
00:35:37,280 --> 00:35:38,480
I brought some refreshments.

479
00:35:39,320 --> 00:35:41,320
Hot coffee and coconut cake.

480
00:35:56,520 --> 00:35:59,160
Hey, Korn.
Take a break and eat some snacks.

481
00:35:59,240 --> 00:36:00,320
Your stomach will hurt again.

482
00:36:01,320 --> 00:36:03,120
No, I'm not hungry yet.

483
00:36:03,880 --> 00:36:05,320
Just one bite.

484
00:36:09,280 --> 00:36:11,520
-What are you doing?
-This one's famous.

485
00:36:11,600 --> 00:36:13,880
I waited in line
early in the morning to buy it.

486
00:36:14,800 --> 00:36:16,600
Ugh, I'm studying.

487
00:36:17,360 --> 00:36:19,800
Come on. Just one bite.

488
00:36:21,600 --> 00:36:23,920
How is it? Want another bite?

489
00:36:28,360 --> 00:36:29,240
Just one, okay?

490
00:36:31,080 --> 00:36:33,000
I'd do anything for my little brother.

491
00:36:37,240 --> 00:36:39,360
I'm grown up already.

492
00:36:42,640 --> 00:36:44,120
-How is it?
-It's pretty good.

493
00:36:44,720 --> 00:36:45,720
I told you.

494
00:36:48,080 --> 00:36:49,240
How far have you gotten?

495
00:36:49,320 --> 00:36:51,480
I just started ratios.

496
00:36:51,560 --> 00:36:52,880
I can't get anything into my head.

497
00:36:53,560 --> 00:36:55,080
Teach me sometime too.

498
00:36:56,560 --> 00:36:57,920
You wouldn't get it.

499
00:37:10,160 --> 00:37:11,080
Just one bite.

500
00:37:13,320 --> 00:37:15,840
Wee, if you don't stop bothering me,

501
00:37:15,920 --> 00:37:17,480
I'll go work somewhere else.

502
00:37:24,040 --> 00:37:26,080
Okay. I won't bother you anymore.

503
00:37:28,280 --> 00:37:29,520
Eat if you're hungry.

504
00:37:30,440 --> 00:37:31,680
Your stomach will act up again.

505
00:38:19,920 --> 00:38:21,960
Alyssa! Alyssa, dear.

506
00:38:22,880 --> 00:38:26,080
Hey, have you seen this news yet?

507
00:38:29,080 --> 00:38:30,640
BREAKING! PIMPA TAYAWAT EXPOSED
AS THE PERSON BEHIND FAKE CSR DONATIONS

508
00:38:31,240 --> 00:38:33,880
It's pretty funny, isn't it?
I just found out my friend

509
00:38:33,960 --> 00:38:36,480
also fell for a fortune teller like this.

510
00:38:38,560 --> 00:38:41,400
I remember you went to see one too,
Aunt Pat.

511
00:38:42,200 --> 00:38:44,560
Oh, Alyssa.

512
00:38:44,640 --> 00:38:46,800
I just went to check it out, that's all.

513
00:38:46,880 --> 00:38:48,520
I didn't actually believe any of that.

514
00:38:49,600 --> 00:38:52,280
Well, but I do think

515
00:38:52,360 --> 00:38:55,960
it's strange.
This happened a long time ago.

516
00:38:56,040 --> 00:38:58,040
It wasn't news back then,

517
00:38:58,120 --> 00:39:00,120
so why did it become news now?

518
00:39:00,920 --> 00:39:03,760
Maybe because fortune teller news
is popular right now.

519
00:39:05,080 --> 00:39:06,720
Or…

520
00:39:07,360 --> 00:39:09,520
Maybe it's a business move.

521
00:39:10,640 --> 00:39:13,840
Pretty dramatic.
It's like the entertainment industry.

522
00:39:20,720 --> 00:39:22,240
I'll wait and see

523
00:39:22,800 --> 00:39:24,520
how Tayawat handles this.

524
00:39:35,080 --> 00:39:36,960
-I'd like to see Mom.
-One moment, please.

525
00:39:42,040 --> 00:39:43,640
Mr. Phakorn would like to see you.

526
00:39:45,000 --> 00:39:46,000
Please come in.

527
00:39:53,120 --> 00:39:55,040
The news spread quickly, Mom.

528
00:39:55,800 --> 00:39:57,160
I have someone looking into it.

529
00:39:58,360 --> 00:39:59,800
What did Grandpa say?

530
00:40:02,240 --> 00:40:05,000
FATHER

531
00:40:08,160 --> 00:40:09,080
Yes, Father.

532
00:40:12,360 --> 00:40:13,360
Okay.

533
00:40:15,520 --> 00:40:16,840
What did Grandpa say?

534
00:40:18,200 --> 00:40:19,600
He wants a press conference.

535
00:40:25,080 --> 00:40:27,400
Taddao, come in here for a moment.

536
00:40:36,760 --> 00:40:37,760
Sorry.

537
00:40:54,560 --> 00:40:56,000
Grandpa went with your idea, Wee.

538
00:40:56,920 --> 00:40:58,480
He decided to hold a press conference.

539
00:41:03,120 --> 00:41:04,960
One voice won over three.

540
00:41:05,840 --> 00:41:08,200
Looks like he really values your opinion.

541
00:41:10,880 --> 00:41:11,840
That's not it.

542
00:41:13,480 --> 00:41:15,120
He made his own decision.

543
00:41:16,080 --> 00:41:18,120
He just wanted to hear different opinions.

544
00:41:22,880 --> 00:41:24,920
Maybe this place suits you more than me.

545
00:41:27,880 --> 00:41:29,360
What exactly do you want, Korn?

546
00:41:32,000 --> 00:41:34,560
Do you want to tell the truth,
or keep things this way?

547
00:41:37,080 --> 00:41:38,680
So I'll know what to do.

548
00:41:43,000 --> 00:41:45,040
I admit that the company

549
00:41:45,640 --> 00:41:47,640
did make a mistake regarding the use

550
00:41:48,440 --> 00:41:50,240
of the CSR budget that year.

551
00:41:52,160 --> 00:41:53,480
Although

552
00:41:54,200 --> 00:41:57,200
this was ultimately a management failure,

553
00:41:57,280 --> 00:41:59,000
as the company's top executive,

554
00:42:00,160 --> 00:42:03,960
I personally take responsibility
for this failure in my duties.

555
00:42:05,160 --> 00:42:06,560
I apologize.

556
00:42:10,200 --> 00:42:12,520
To show the company's sincerity,

557
00:42:13,240 --> 00:42:14,480
we will donate

558
00:42:15,440 --> 00:42:16,960
an amount

559
00:42:17,720 --> 00:42:19,440
equal to that year's CSR budget

560
00:42:20,640 --> 00:42:23,360
as scholarships
for underprivileged schools

561
00:42:24,680 --> 00:42:26,680
and purchase medical equipment

562
00:42:27,400 --> 00:42:30,280
for underprivileged hospitals as well.

563
00:42:35,960 --> 00:42:39,560
As for the unintentional mistake
made by my eldest daughter,

564
00:42:39,640 --> 00:42:41,280
I have removed her from her position

565
00:42:42,320 --> 00:42:44,920
and she will no longer be involved
in management,

566
00:42:47,160 --> 00:42:49,360
to prevent similar mistakes in the future.

567
00:42:51,080 --> 00:42:52,320
Our company

568
00:42:52,920 --> 00:42:54,840
has always been committed to quality.

569
00:42:56,360 --> 00:42:57,880
Every house we have sold,

570
00:42:58,840 --> 00:43:00,600
every condo project we have developed,

571
00:43:01,840 --> 00:43:02,960
are proof of that.

572
00:43:05,160 --> 00:43:07,880
We have always taken
the best care of our customers,

573
00:43:08,840 --> 00:43:10,400
and we will continue

574
00:43:11,200 --> 00:43:13,320
to take the best care of society as well.

575
00:43:15,560 --> 00:43:17,760
That concludes this press conference.

576
00:43:36,720 --> 00:43:37,960
Nada!

577
00:43:47,520 --> 00:43:48,680
Nada.

578
00:44:00,120 --> 00:44:01,600
Congratulations, Aunt Da.

579
00:44:01,680 --> 00:44:03,640
The press conference was well received.

580
00:44:04,480 --> 00:44:07,200
They're beautiful. Thank you, Alyssa.

581
00:44:11,000 --> 00:44:12,200
Come, have a seat.

582
00:44:20,760 --> 00:44:23,520
Actually, today's press conference

583
00:44:23,600 --> 00:44:25,120
was Rawee's idea.

584
00:44:25,720 --> 00:44:28,200
At first, we were going to stay quiet,

585
00:44:28,280 --> 00:44:30,640
but Rawee
suggested holding a press conference

586
00:44:30,720 --> 00:44:32,400
and making an additional donation.

587
00:44:35,320 --> 00:44:37,800
That was definitely the right decision.

588
00:44:44,920 --> 00:44:46,520
Oh, Rawee.

589
00:44:53,800 --> 00:44:55,760
The documents after the press conference.

590
00:45:01,760 --> 00:45:05,640
Rawee, we were just talking
about today's press conference.

591
00:45:05,720 --> 00:45:08,600
Alyssa said
the response was very positive,

592
00:45:08,680 --> 00:45:10,600
so I told her it was your work.

593
00:45:11,120 --> 00:45:12,320
Thank you very much.

594
00:45:14,680 --> 00:45:16,280
If my father knew,

595
00:45:16,360 --> 00:45:18,600
he'd definitely try to get you back.

596
00:45:19,640 --> 00:45:21,600
Looks like we'll have to fight for him,
Alyssa.

597
00:45:23,240 --> 00:45:24,400
It's not that big a deal.

598
00:45:35,640 --> 00:45:36,840
Where did Phakorn go?

599
00:45:40,760 --> 00:45:42,240
Maybe he went to the restroom.

600
00:45:43,280 --> 00:45:44,480
I'll call him.

601
00:46:00,600 --> 00:46:01,840
He's not answering.

602
00:46:02,440 --> 00:46:04,160
Do you two have plans after this?

603
00:46:05,480 --> 00:46:08,400
No. I only came today
to bring you flowers,

604
00:46:08,480 --> 00:46:10,160
then I was going to leave.

605
00:46:11,600 --> 00:46:13,640
It's almost time to get off work.

606
00:46:14,640 --> 00:46:16,320
Mr. Rawee, are you going back together?

607
00:46:19,200 --> 00:46:20,760
Are you going back to Chonburi?

608
00:46:21,760 --> 00:46:22,600
No.

609
00:46:22,680 --> 00:46:24,440
I'm actually renting a house
from Mr. Nimit

610
00:46:24,520 --> 00:46:26,600
in the same village as Ms. Alyssa.

611
00:46:30,560 --> 00:46:32,440
It's okay. I can go back on my own.

612
00:46:34,920 --> 00:46:38,240
That's nice.
Everything is such a coincidence.

613
00:46:40,160 --> 00:46:42,200
-Then I'll get going.
-Alright.

614
00:46:42,280 --> 00:46:43,200
Goodbye.

615
00:46:48,760 --> 00:46:49,800
I'll excuse myself as well.

616
00:47:16,840 --> 00:47:18,520
What did Grandpa say?

617
00:47:20,000 --> 00:47:21,280
He wants a press conference.

618
00:47:26,800 --> 00:47:28,760
One voice won over three.

619
00:47:29,600 --> 00:47:31,840
Looks like he really values your opinion.

620
00:47:33,000 --> 00:47:34,280
That's not it.

621
00:47:35,560 --> 00:47:37,120
He made his own decision.

622
00:47:38,240 --> 00:47:40,120
He just wanted to hear different opinions.

623
00:47:41,240 --> 00:47:43,320
Maybe this place suits you more than me.

624
00:47:48,120 --> 00:47:51,160
Alyssa said
the response was very positive,

625
00:47:51,240 --> 00:47:53,600
so I told her it was your work.

626
00:47:53,680 --> 00:47:54,760
Thank you very much.

627
00:47:54,840 --> 00:47:56,640
<i>If my father knew,</i>

628
00:47:56,720 --> 00:47:59,120
<i>he'd definitely try to get you back.</i>

629
00:47:59,200 --> 00:48:01,320
Looks like we'll have to fight for him,
Alyssa.

630
00:48:01,400 --> 00:48:02,360
Yes.

631
00:48:03,080 --> 00:48:04,080
It's not that big a deal.

632
00:48:11,400 --> 00:48:13,680
RAWEE

633
00:48:45,480 --> 00:48:47,760
RAWEE

634
00:48:53,960 --> 00:48:56,200
Hey, bring me another glass.

635
00:49:17,240 --> 00:49:18,160
Can you handle it?

636
00:49:19,640 --> 00:49:20,560
I can.

637
00:49:21,160 --> 00:49:24,480
You've already had quite a few.
Are you sure you can drive home?

638
00:49:25,320 --> 00:49:28,320
Let me drive you home.
Then you can drink as much as you want.

639
00:49:29,880 --> 00:49:31,040
I have a girlfriend.

640
00:49:34,320 --> 00:49:37,320
Your girlfriend's name is Rawee?

641
00:49:38,280 --> 00:49:40,160
No way. That's my brother.

642
00:49:42,080 --> 00:49:44,280
I've only seen
someone named Rawee calling you.

643
00:49:44,360 --> 00:49:46,480
I haven't seen anyone else
checking on you.

644
00:49:51,120 --> 00:49:54,920
PHAKORN (14)

645
00:50:03,640 --> 00:50:05,920
RAWEE

646
00:50:36,360 --> 00:50:38,160
PHAKORN

647
00:50:43,840 --> 00:50:45,320
What are you doing?

648
00:50:46,240 --> 00:50:47,600
I was about to go to sleep.

649
00:50:48,200 --> 00:50:50,040
Can you come get me?

650
00:50:51,320 --> 00:50:53,000
I'm really drunk.

651
00:50:54,880 --> 00:50:57,120
Where are you?

652
00:50:57,200 --> 00:50:59,240
If you don't come,

653
00:50:59,920 --> 00:51:01,720
I'll just sleep here.

654
00:51:03,760 --> 00:51:06,840
Fine. It's up to you.
Sleep at the bar if you want.

655
00:51:17,920 --> 00:51:19,080
Sir.

656
00:51:22,040 --> 00:51:23,480
The bar is closing soon.

657
00:51:26,000 --> 00:51:27,120
Give me one more glass.

658
00:51:36,480 --> 00:51:38,720
Whoa! Careful, Sir.

659
00:51:41,240 --> 00:51:43,640
-Just walk me to my car.
-Oh.

660
00:51:43,720 --> 00:51:46,360
Look at you.
You can't drive home like this.

661
00:51:46,440 --> 00:51:47,880
Let me take you home, okay?

662
00:51:54,720 --> 00:51:56,000
Alyssa.

663
00:51:57,240 --> 00:51:58,480
Is she your girlfriend?

664
00:52:00,600 --> 00:52:02,240
Did you come to pick me up?

665
00:52:04,320 --> 00:52:06,160
-Get in the car.
-Okay.

666
00:52:18,400 --> 00:52:20,120
Tell me.

667
00:52:20,200 --> 00:52:22,960
What got you so stressed
that you drank this much?

668
00:52:25,400 --> 00:52:27,440
Whenever you're angry,
you start talking like this.

669
00:52:32,480 --> 00:52:35,120
You're an adult now
and your health isn't good enough

670
00:52:35,200 --> 00:52:36,720
to drink this heavily.

671
00:52:44,800 --> 00:52:48,720
I was just in my room,
stressed and overthinking.

672
00:52:52,000 --> 00:52:53,880
You called me out this late at night.

673
00:52:54,520 --> 00:52:57,720
If I hadn't come,
you would've gone home with her, right?

674
00:53:02,520 --> 00:53:04,080
Are you jealous?

675
00:53:07,640 --> 00:53:09,880
Don't change the subject, okay?
I'm still mad.

676
00:53:11,800 --> 00:53:15,080
I'm sorry. I won't do it again.

677
00:53:17,480 --> 00:53:18,520
Okay.

678
00:53:19,440 --> 00:53:21,560
Now tell me. What's stressing you out?

679
00:53:29,280 --> 00:53:30,320
Well,

680
00:53:31,360 --> 00:53:32,680
I just feel like…

681
00:53:34,600 --> 00:53:36,200
I'm not that important.

682
00:53:36,800 --> 00:53:38,600
Not important to who?

683
00:53:40,200 --> 00:53:41,160
To me?

684
00:53:42,600 --> 00:53:44,080
Or at the company?

685
00:53:48,160 --> 00:53:50,760
It's about Mr. Rawee's idea, isn't it?

686
00:53:52,400 --> 00:53:54,800
Did I make you feel that way?

687
00:53:59,400 --> 00:54:00,440
Uh…

688
00:54:01,200 --> 00:54:02,520
It's Grandpa.

689
00:54:07,360 --> 00:54:09,040
I just feel upset

690
00:54:09,880 --> 00:54:12,520
that my opinions always get overlooked.

691
00:54:23,080 --> 00:54:24,440
You know, right?

692
00:54:24,520 --> 00:54:26,920
That you can tell me anything.

693
00:54:29,400 --> 00:54:30,240
Thank you.

694
00:54:31,480 --> 00:54:33,240
Thank you for making me realize

695
00:54:34,760 --> 00:54:36,480
that I still matter to you.

696
00:54:48,640 --> 00:54:50,040
But I'm afraid

697
00:54:52,640 --> 00:54:55,480
you'll find someone better than me.

698
00:54:59,480 --> 00:55:01,120
Why would you say that?

699
00:55:13,960 --> 00:55:14,920
Oh.

700
00:55:17,480 --> 00:55:19,400
This is my hat.

701
00:55:20,200 --> 00:55:21,760
You've kept it here this whole time?

702
00:55:24,000 --> 00:55:26,360
I was waiting for you
to return my hair tie.

703
00:55:27,080 --> 00:55:29,280
It's been so long.
When are you going to give it back?

704
00:55:32,560 --> 00:55:35,400
Then let me keep it for now.

705
00:55:37,800 --> 00:55:40,680
Until you agree to be my girlfriend.

706
00:55:43,160 --> 00:55:46,440
And what if I don't say yes?

707
00:55:49,640 --> 00:55:50,760
Then…

708
00:55:55,920 --> 00:55:57,480
I can wait my whole life.

709
00:56:21,480 --> 00:56:22,480
I'm sorry.

710
00:56:26,400 --> 00:56:27,480
Go get some sleep.

711
00:56:28,200 --> 00:56:30,520
You have to go out of town early tomorrow.

712
00:56:36,800 --> 00:56:37,720
Okay.

713
00:56:39,040 --> 00:56:40,960
I'll head in now.

714
00:56:41,720 --> 00:56:45,480
When you get home,
don't forget to text me.

715
00:56:51,720 --> 00:56:52,640
Good night.

716
00:56:54,000 --> 00:56:55,040
Good night.

717
00:57:29,480 --> 00:57:31,160
I didn't think anything of it.

718
00:57:31,240 --> 00:57:33,960
I understand that Alyssa is kind

719
00:57:34,040 --> 00:57:35,480
<i>and down-to-earth.</i>

720
00:57:37,440 --> 00:57:39,120
<i>I'm more worried about you.</i>

721
00:57:40,840 --> 00:57:42,680
I really didn't think
anything of it, Korn.

722
00:57:43,640 --> 00:57:45,200
I trust you, Wee.

723
00:57:46,520 --> 00:57:49,200
Father, Da has been shot.

724
00:57:49,920 --> 00:57:52,200
-What did you say?
-Da has been shot.

725
00:57:52,280 --> 00:57:53,920
<i>The patient has lost a lot of blood.</i>

726
00:57:54,000 --> 00:57:55,680
Does anyone share Ms. Nada's blood type?

727
00:57:55,760 --> 00:57:57,160
Rawee does.

728
00:57:57,240 --> 00:58:00,720
How do you know
Mr. Rawee's blood type matches Aunt Da's?

729
00:58:01,760 --> 00:58:05,440
I need the DNA test results.
Please help me.

730
00:58:05,520 --> 00:58:08,480
For Ms. Nada and Mr. Phakorn, right?

731
00:58:08,560 --> 00:58:10,200
Include Rawee too.

732
00:58:10,280 --> 00:58:11,960
I've been suspicious for a long time

733
00:58:12,040 --> 00:58:13,880
about why Nada

734
00:58:13,960 --> 00:58:15,720
refused a DNA test.

735
00:58:15,800 --> 00:58:18,840
She must be hiding something.

736
00:58:52,080 --> 00:58:54,080
Subtitle translation by:
Chomchanach Yanaharn
